// ————— Your tsumiki journey: the tower, the build, and the map —————
// HAND-MAINTAINED. Not generated by build-vite-app.py.
//
// The screen behind docs/design/rework/12-journey.html, which Lloyd approved
// Oct 6 2026. The board is the spec for how this LOOKS; lib/blocks.js is where
// blocks come from and how they sync. This file only draws.
//
// ⚠️ THE STANDING RULES, every one of which this screen can break by accident:
//   · A block is EFFORT, never grading. No verdict colour, no correction, ever —
//     a checker block shows its sentence exactly as written.
//   · Nothing falls, decays or greys out. The tower never shrinks. Dimming
//     exists only while a filter is on.
//   · No counts, no targets, no "next", no locked silhouettes, no unlit map
//     points. A structure is announced in the past tense, once already earned,
//     and the next one is never previewed.
//   · No calendar grid and no day-rows. A date appears only when a block is
//     tapped.
//   · Colour is never the only signal: every section mark carries its glyph.
//
// Map outline: Natural Earth 1:50m Admin 0, v4.1.0 (public domain), via the npm
// package world-atlas@2.0.2 (countries-50m.json, Japan id 392), cropped to
// 128.6–146.0°E / 30.0–45.6°N, equirectangular scaled by cos 37.5°, simplified
// (Ramer–Douglas–Peucker, 0.45px). Inlined; nothing is fetched at runtime.
// Okinawa and the outlying islands are not drawn at this scale — an inset box
// is the answer if a site is ever placed there.

